{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat upon the blood.</b> It is expounded in many ways in Sanhedrin (63a); this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 19:26). And what emerges from there according to the sugya is that they are all from the Torah, for the verse included every eating of blood in one negative commandment. If so, what the verse says concerning Saul (I Samuel 14:33), \"Behold, the people are sinning against YHWH, to eat upon the blood\" — they were sinning in one of the categories subsumed under this prohibition, for they were eating from the animal before its soul had departed. This is what it says (ibid. v. 32), \"And the people flew upon the spoil\" — like a bird of prey that swoops and eats — \"and they took sheep and cattle, etc., and slaughtered them on the ground, and the people ate upon the blood\": because of the abundance of spoil in livestock, when they would pour their blood on the ground, they would tear off their limbs and eat them before they died. And according to the plain sense, it is a type of sorcery or divination, for it is something learned from its context, and they would pour the blood and gather it in a pit, and the demons would gather there according to their notion and eat from their table, to tell them the future. And when Israel was with Saul in that camp, they were very frightened of the Philistines, and Saul would do nothing other than inquire through Urim and Thummim, as it is said (ibid. v. 36), \"Let us draw near here to Elohim,\" and the people would inquire through demons or through sorcery to know their way and their actions, and they would eat upon the blood to perform that deed. Therefore the verse says (ibid. v. 33), \"And they told Saul, saying: Behold, the people are sinning against YHWH, to eat upon the blood. And he said: You have acted treacherously\" — to say: Behold, HaShem has wrought a great deliverance for you today, yet you inquire of no elohim — this is treachery. And I will further explain the prohibition of the soothsayer and the diviner (Deuteronomy 18:9)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:56:29.072576463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}